      "title": "Delete user route lacks admin check",
      "description": "The DELETE /users/:id route has no requireAdmin middleware. Its sibling routes in the same router both use requireAdmin. Any caller who reaches the server can delete any user by id. Attackers can enumerate ids to wipe accounts. Add requireAdmin to the route before the handler.",
      "suggested_change": "admin.delete(\"/users/:id\", requireAdmin, async (req, res) => {",
      "source": "lens:id-enumeration-sequential",
      "candidate": null,
      "notes": [],
      "problem": "The DELETE /users/:id route has no requireAdmin middleware. Its sibling routes in the same router both use requireAdmin.",
      "consequence": "Any caller who reaches the server can delete any user by id. Attackers can enumerate ids to wipe accounts.",
      "fix": "Add requireAdmin to the route before the handler."
    },
    {
      "origin": "agent",
      "severity": "major",
      "category": "bug",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "file_path": "src/admin.js",
      "line_number": 22,
      "line_end": 25,
      "title": "Purge drops removal promises and reports success early",
      "description": "The purge handler passes an async callback to forEach, so nobody awaits or catches the removeUser promises. db.removeUser throws for an unknown id, which causes an unhandled rejection. One unknown id can crash the Node process through the unhandled rejection. The handler also reports every id as removed before any deletion finishes or fails. Await Promise.allSettled over ids.map(removeUser). Then report the count of fulfilled results.",
      "suggested_change": "  const results = await Promise.allSettled(ids.map((id) => db.removeUser(id)));\n  res.json({ removed: results.filter((r) => r.status === \"fulfilled\").length });",
      "source": "lens:async-floating-promise",
      "candidate": null,
      "notes": [],
      "problem": "The purge handler passes an async callback to forEach, so nobody awaits or catches the removeUser promises. db.removeUser throws for an unknown id, which causes an unhandled rejection.",
      "consequence": "One unknown id can crash the Node process through the unhandled rejection. The handler also reports every id as removed before any deletion finishes or fails.",
      "fix": "Await Promise.allSettled over ids.map(removeUser). Then report the count of fulfilled results."
    },
    {
